WEBVTT

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:05.980
Two Weeks Before the Harvest Festival

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:39.510
Moyashimon

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.510
Returns

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:05.980
Fermenting Cellar

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.980
Malt Cellar 2

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:14.140
It's miso time, you moldy 
little chicken shits!

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:15.230
If I catch you slacking off,

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:18.170
I'll make miso sauce 
out of you! Mayonnaise!

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:19.490
Sir, yes, sir!

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.470
Do you understand, you moldy 
little chicken shits?!

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:24.490
That sergeant is as tough as ever.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.100
Sir, yes, sir!

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:26.220
Then tell me what you understand!

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:28.200
They're all doing a good 
job because of it, though.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:29.480
Come on, now! I can't hear you!

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:31.250
Yeah, no unwanted microbes are 
propagating, so it's going well.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:31.500
Mayonnaise!

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:34.230
But you're having a hard time 
too, aren't you, Tadayasu?

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:32.900
Sir, yes, sir!

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:34.400
Mayonnaise!

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:37.430
You're doing almost all 
the work in malt cellar 2.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:35.980
Sir, yes, sir!

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:39.010
I have no choice.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:42.780
Oikawa and Mutou-san have their 
hands full with malt cellar 1.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:45.570
We don't even know where Hasegawa-san is.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.770
And I can't get in touch with 
Misato-san or Kawahama-san.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:53.530
What are Hasegawa, Misato, 
and Kawahama doing?

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:55.770
And the harvest festival starts tomorrow!

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.240
Misato-san

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.240
Misato-san

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:01.800
Misato-san?

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:04.420
Hello?

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:06.200
Hey, long time no talk.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.930
Where are you?

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:09.030
Never mind that.

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:10.300
We're meeting tomorrow at 9am

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.700
in front of the fermenting cellar.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:12.600
Huh?

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:14.350
Like I told you before,

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:17.000
the fermenting cellar crew 
is going to run a stall.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.700
We need you to help out.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:21.270
See you there.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:26.260
At least they've been working on 
getting the stall ready, I guess.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.020
Well? Think it'll be ready in time?

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:31.270
Yeah, no problem.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:43.030
The 
Next 
Day

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:48.580
I'm Rice 
Plant-chan.

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:49.040
78th Annual University Harvest Festival

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:49.040
I'm Rice 
Plant-kun.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:46.250
<i>The Harvest Festival Committee</i>

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:49.440
<i>would like to request that all visitors</i>

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:52.240
<i>please wait patiently, as crowding</i>

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:53.390
You've gotta be kidding!

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.610
<i>the gate is very dangerous.</i>

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:55.200
This is ridiculous!

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.720
Just open up already!

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:58.380
What are you thinking?!

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.680
The gate opens at 10 o'clock.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:06.010
Please remain in line and don't crowd.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:09.220
Free produce will be distributed on 
a first come, first served basis,

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:12.540
but don't worry, we have 
enough for everyone.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:14.290
Don't make us wait!

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:15.720
Just open up already!

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:16.910
Hurry it up!

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:18.570
What are you thinking?!

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:24.570
No 
Climbing

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:24.550
Free Produce Line 
Ends Here

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:26.250
I was here first!

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:28.280
No, I was!

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:31.210
This harvest festival is intense.

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:33.610
Way too different from 
the spring festival.

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:35.290
Scary!

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:38.030
All students, please enter the

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:40.350
university grounds through the back gate.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:45.300
Student Entrance  
Please Present Student ID

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:43.540
Repeat: all students, 
please enter the

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:45.300
university grounds through the back gate.

00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:57.800
Sawaki-kun!

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:00.810
Oikawa...

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:04.710
Want a lift?

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:06.410
You're headed to the 
fermenting cellar, right?

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:09.070
Yeah. Did Misato-san and 
Kawahama-san call you, too?

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:14.260
Yes! They said to leave 
the stall to them,

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:16.710
then suddenly this morning, 
they asked me to run it for them!

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:18.690
What's with that look, anyway?

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:21.440
I was at karaoke all night with Aya-san.

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:23.750
What the hell? Why didn't you invite me?

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:25.820
Just get on. We've gotta hurry.

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:26.680
Okay.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:48.490
Miss Agricultural University's Bar 
Aoi's Bar

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:47.160
Aoi's...

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:48.490
...Bar?

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:51.990
Miss Agricultural University's Bar

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:51.990
Aoi's Bar

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:50.440
Here they are!

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:51.990
You guys are late!

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:00.000
What is "Aoi's Bar," anyway?

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:03.970
We're gonna sell the liquor we've 
been working on for a while.

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:06.130
Sorry, but we're confident in these.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:08.240
You mean those?

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:09.260
Yep.

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:15.340
Are those even drinkable?

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:17.080
It better not be the kind you 
chew up before fermenting.

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:18.230
Of course not.

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:20.270
And what's the point of Aoi's Bar?

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:23.300
Mutou also mentioned it, 
so I'm sure you know,

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:27.680
but the stall that is the most 
popular at the harvest festival

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:30.030
wins prize money regardless 
of their lab or circle.

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:33.640
We figured more people 
would buy our liquor

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:37.290
if we used Miss Agricultural University, 
Mutou-san, on our sign.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:39.980
And where is Mutou-san?

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:43.250
Apparently she was drinking with 
Professor Itsuki last night,

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:44.710
so she's sleeping in the cellar.

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:52.260
Morning already?

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:55.560
I gotta get dressed.

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:59.690
Huh? My clothes...

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:06.090
Your clothes are in the wash. 
Wear this instead.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:15.580
Oh, come on... a bunny?

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:18.080
And it's the harvest festival...

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.080
Guess I have no choice.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:24.080
Like hell I don't! Where are my clothes?!

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:35.600
Free Produce Distribution

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.830
<i>This is an announcement to all students</i>

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:30.330
<i>from the agricultural society.</i>

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:32.520
<i>The gate opens in five minutes.</i>

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:36.360
<i>All students, please stand 
by in your positions.</i>

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:40.030
<i>Please do not leave your positions.</i>

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:43.600
Agricultural Society

00:07:40.030 --> 00:07:40.900
Ready?

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:43.600
If they actually attack, 
worry about yourself first.

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:47.680
We're going to avenge 
our senpais this year.

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:48.700
Got it?

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:53.520
Listen up! Our role at 
this harvest festival

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:56.150
is to keep the housewives, 
rushing the stalls

00:07:56.150 --> 00:07:58.260
for free produce, in their lines!

00:07:58.260 --> 00:07:58.870
Right!

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:02.090
Free; produce; first come, first served:

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:04.680
Never underestimate a housewife's 
drive when these terms are involved.

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:05.380
Right!

00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:08.690
They attack with the same 
force as the Kwansei offense!

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:10.180
Th-They're that strong?

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:11.270
Yes.

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:12.660
If one gets past you, stop her as though

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:14.170
she were going for the winning touchdown!

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:15.340
Right!

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:19.390
We are the keepers of order 
at this harvest festival!

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:22.350
Each man must defend his 
position to the death!

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:23.390
Right!

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:28.650
It's time.

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:32.150
<i>It's 10 o'clock. We will now open the gate.</i>

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:34.570
<i>We will now open the gate.</i>

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:40.960
This is our Koshien Bowl!

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:42.250
Prepare to risk your lives!

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:45.540
Looks like the festival's starting.

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:47.190
They'll go for the produce first.

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:49.170
The food stalls won't start 
getting crowded until later.

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:54.270
I'm not really sure why, 
but I'm getting nervous.

00:08:54.270 --> 00:08:55.050
Yeah.

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:58.050
Free Produce Distribution

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:00.750
It's just about time.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:02.000
We're counting on you guys!

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.560
Football team! Lacrosse team!

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:05.580
Here they come.

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:06.560
Right!

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:08.900
Please stay in line

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:10.990
Formation!

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:16.420
The fate of our university 
rests on this battle!

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:18.700
Each of you, give it all you've got!

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.700
Please stay in line

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:20.680
Right!

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:26.970
You're in charge of daikon.

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:29.180
Got it. And you go for the fruits.

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:30.000
Leave it to me!

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.790
Be sure to get rice, 
no matter how heavy it is!

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:35.490
The football team tells us 
every year to stay in line,

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:36.870
so the first step is to crush them.

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:39.470
Okay! I'll knock out the little guys!

00:09:39.490 --> 00:09:41.970
78th Annual Agricultural University Harvest Festival

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:41.890
<i>The 78th Annual</i>

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:45.980
<i>Agricultural University Harvest 
Festival will now begin.</i>

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:45.980
One, two...

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:49.860
Please proceed slowly and—

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:15.440
<i>We have arrived at</i>

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:18.320
<i>Charles de Gaulle 
International Airport in Paris.</i>

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:21.520
<i>Please remain seated until the</i>

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:24.240
<i>aircraft comes to a complete stop.</i>

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:28.720
<i>The local time is 3:00 AM.</i>

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:30.590
<i>The weather is clear.</i>

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:33.550
The harvest festival has started.

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:44.790
Move it!

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.120
Out of the way!

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:48.120
My well-being depends on this!

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:51.420
Go!

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:22.430
Please 
stay in line

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:25.260
Instant defeat again this year...

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:32.500
Put out some onions!

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:34.960
This is nowhere near enough!

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:36.710
Get more vegetables out here, now!

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:39.270
We can tear down the 
tent and just rush them!

00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:44.270
They must be running out of produce now.

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:47.510
Yeah. They should be heading this way.

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:49.490
Hey...

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:51.480
What?

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:55.220
What is this white stuff in the barrels?

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:56.980
That's pulque.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.270
Pulque?

00:11:58.270 --> 00:11:59.490
A Mexican liquor.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:03.870
Mexico is famous for tequila, 
the liquor made by distilling

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:06.130
the sap of agave plants.

00:12:06.130 --> 00:12:09.450
But there is another type 
of agave called maguey,

00:12:06.260 --> 00:12:12.000
Types of Maguey (AKA Agave) and the Liquors Made from Them

00:12:06.260 --> 00:12:12.000
Used for Mezcal               Used for Pulque                 Used for Tequila

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:12.000
which is used to make unrefined pulque.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:15.970
I thought tequila was 
made from orchid flowers.

00:12:15.970 --> 00:12:18.000
So it's made from sap, not flowers?

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:22.200
Yes, and agave has the 
 kanji for orchid in its name,

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:24.530
but it looks more like a cactus.

00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:27.420
To explain the making of 
pulque in simple terms,

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:30.120
aguamiel is collected from maguey.

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:32.730
Well, in the old days they used acocote.

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:36.520
And semilla is then 
made from the aguamiel.

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:38.220
Excuse me...

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:40.670
I have no idea what you just said.

00:12:40.670 --> 00:12:42.270
Same as the guy to my right.

00:12:42.270 --> 00:12:44.530
Leave it to a returnee from Mexico.

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:48.210
Well, anyway, the semilla 
is portioned out for reserves,

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:51.110
and then aguamiel is added again.

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:53.540
Right, I get it now. Thanks.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:56.490
Let's brew!

00:12:56.490 --> 00:12:57.760
Let's brew!

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:00.550
We haven't had much action yet.

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:03.780
Looks like lactic acid bacteria 
are the most prominent.

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:05.410
There isn't much cerevisiae.

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:08.550
Yeah, you're right. 
There's not much alcohol content.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:11.220
They all look the same inside.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:13.060
Why do they have different labels?

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:16.890
Pulque comes in various names 
depending on the alcohol content.

00:13:16.890 --> 00:13:18.540
The one with the highest content is fuerte,

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:20.540
and the one with the lowest is suave.

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:22.070
That seems kind of sketchy.

00:13:22.390 --> 00:13:25.570
It is. That's how liquors are.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:35.510
Free to Take

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:29.500
Pulque isn't even widely manufactured.

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:31.030
It's just made by old guys

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:33.550
around town and sold from their homes.

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:35.010
Fill this up with pulque.

00:13:35.010 --> 00:13:36.080
Sure.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:41.570
Unrefined liquors only need to be 
there for local folks to enjoy.

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:44.060
That's exactly why even a 
cheap liquor like this

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:46.050
is so deeply rooted in the nation's culture.

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:50.600
Wow, so this stuff is really 
that well known in Mexico?

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:52.840
Oh, uh, just to add...

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:55.600
Things like tequila, rum, and Corona beer

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:57.890
are more popular even in Mexico.

00:13:57.890 --> 00:13:58.660
Oh.

00:13:58.660 --> 00:13:59.610
Really?

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:02.650
This is just a drink for kids.

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:04.860
Kids aren't supposed to drink alcohol.

00:14:05.210 --> 00:14:07.490
Still, making liquor from sap...

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:10.430
People will really make 
liquor from anything, huh?

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:12.550
That's right, as long 
as there's sugar in it.

00:14:12.550 --> 00:14:14.600
Whether it's persimmons, 
tomatoes, or even cola,

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:16.920
yeast will turn it into alcohol.

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:18.840
This maguey sap tastes somewhat

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:21.880
like maple syrup when concentrated.

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:25.180
It's a sap that rhinoceros beetles love.

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:27.380
No human could hate it.

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:27.380
Beetle

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:29.880
Well...

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:30.890
What?

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:34.360
Sorry, but we'll be leaving the stall to

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:36.410
you two and Mutou-san now.

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:37.390
What?!

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:40.900
Kawahama and I have a little 
business to attend to.

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:42.840
How can you be so lax?

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:43.900
You're going somewhere?

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:47.900
We're a little more active 
when Hasegawa isn't around.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:50.900
Okay, Oikawa, you sell the pulque,

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:53.450
and Sawaki, you regulate the fermenting.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:54.160
Regulate?

00:14:54.180 --> 00:15:01.650
Pineapple

00:14:54.180 --> 00:15:01.650
Guava

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:57.300
If it ferments too much 
and starts to taste weird,

00:14:57.300 --> 00:14:59.570
add those pineapple 
and guava juices to it

00:14:59.570 --> 00:15:01.670
and sell it for 50 yen more.

00:15:02.190 --> 00:15:04.040
That's regulating it?

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:06.010
We're counting on you guys!

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:07.570
No bailing out!

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:13.000
I guess they really are hopeless 
without Hasegawa-san.

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:15.030
They're so quick to skip out on work.

00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:24.250
It looks the same every year.

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:25.570
Yeah.

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:29.950
Medieval Europe Research Club
Grilled Foods

00:15:26.510 --> 00:15:30.200
The Medieval Europe research
club is doing that again?

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:33.200
A whole roasted pig!

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:36.700
Demonstration sales three times a day!

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:40.260
Try some healthy ice 
cream made with soybeans!

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:41.470
Would you like a university 
brand bamboo fiber shirt?

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:42.320
Soybean juice over here!

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:44.710
Try some delicious bean 
curry with soybeans!

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:46.800
Parents and Kids Can Make It Together!
 Natto Classroom

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:48.710
This is the homemade natto classroom!

00:15:49.270 --> 00:15:51.240
Who wants to have fun making 
natto with the family,

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:54.220
using soybeans and straw 
grown here at the university?

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:56.720
Soybean Soup

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:56.720
Would you like some soybean soup?

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:59.730
Soybean Ramen

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:59.730
Soybean ramen! Soybean ramen here!

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:03.570
A lot of soybean stalls 
this year, aren't there?

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:06.190
We had a big soybean harvest this year.

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:09.230
The agricultural society pushed 
people to sell soybean products.

00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:11.240
Soybean juice here!

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:13.740
Care for a healthy soybean bento?

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:18.580
Mom! There's nothing but soybeans!

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:29.170
Welcome! Help yourself!

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:29.170
Delicious Please Eat

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:29.580
We've got lots of foods smuggled in

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:31.180
for us by our exchange 
student, Chapai-kun,

00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:33.380
that have never been on 
Japanese soil before!

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:35.920
Come enjoy a meal from a foreign land!

00:16:35.920 --> 00:16:37.340
The hell is that?

00:16:40.400 --> 00:16:42.290
There they are.

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:45.170
Misato, Kawahama.

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:47.270
We've got the info.

00:16:47.680 --> 00:16:50.380
So who is this year's live guest?

00:16:50.380 --> 00:16:52.780
It's Tanaka Kyoko.

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:54.280
Tanaka Kyoko?

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:57.190
She's appeared on golden 
time variety shows.

00:16:57.190 --> 00:16:59.110
She's pretty famous.

00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:01.510
So there must be a demand...

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:02.470
Yeah.

00:17:02.470 --> 00:17:04.900
You're certain about this?

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:05.790
There's no mistake.

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:07.790
Idol Club 
President

00:17:06.740 --> 00:17:09.640
The idol club witnessed 
TanaKyo introducing

00:17:09.640 --> 00:17:11.800
herself to the agricultural society.

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:13.800
Nice to meet you!

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:15.220
She's so thin!

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:16.300
So cute!

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:18.640
That would make her the main event

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:20.310
for the night of the festival, then.

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:21.460
Indeed.

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:26.110
Damn it! Where did 
Misato and Kawahama go?

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:27.940
Give me back my clothes!

00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:31.190
Sorry for the wait. 
Customer number 14, please.

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:34.860
Okay... two beers and 
three pulque, right?

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:36.140
Coming right up.

00:17:36.140 --> 00:17:40.700
Hey, why do I have to work 
at Aoi's Bar in my pajamas?!

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:42.950
And it's so busy!

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:43.700
I'm parched here!

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:45.950
Bring those two back here!

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:46.710
Hurry it up!

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:49.430
And, Souemon, what are you doing?!

00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:50.710
Yeah! Get to work!

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:52.550
I am working!

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:54.470
I'm regulating the fermentation!

00:17:54.470 --> 00:17:56.970
Yay! Let's brew!

00:17:57.550 --> 00:18:00.010
Darn it, as soon as I 
realized it was warming up,

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:02.020
it started to ferment all of a sudden!

00:18:02.020 --> 00:18:04.480
It's gonna lose its 
sweetness at this rate!

00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:06.870
Hey, you guys, chill out!

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:07.640
Huh?

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:09.480
Don't change the flavor of the pulque!

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:12.350
What does that homo sapiens 
think he's saying?

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:15.160
We're not making liquor, 
we're making a living!

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:16.040
Idiot!

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:19.450
Try putting yourself in our shoes,

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:21.300
having to live in barely-sweet 
stuff like this!

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:24.500
Go ahead and pour that juice 
into the tanks if you want!

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:28.380
Quit grumbling and get to work, Tadayasu!

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:30.180
I am working!

00:18:30.180 --> 00:18:32.220
In fact, I'm facing a dilemma right now!

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:35.270
What dilemma? 
All you're doing is grumbling!

00:18:35.270 --> 00:18:38.640
Or are you going to tell me you 
were talking with microbes?!

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:41.220
Tell her you were, Tadayasu!

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:42.350
Tell her, tell her!

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:44.520
Anyway, it won't stop fermenting!

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:47.020
Our line of customers 
isn't stopping, either!

00:18:49.720 --> 00:18:51.400
Okay, stop!

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:54.020
Everyone curb the anger! 
We need to chill!

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:55.550
Hurry up!

00:18:55.090 --> 00:18:56.460
Are we there yet?

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:58.070
Why isn't the line moving?

00:18:58.360 --> 00:18:59.930
Come on!

00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:01.970
How long do we have to wait?

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:02.890
Coming!

00:19:02.890 --> 00:19:04.030
So sorry!

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:07.380
That's it... there's 
no one to take charge.

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:08.860
Researcher Hasegawa...

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:09.980
Where are you?

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:11.920
So the princess really is gone.

00:19:12.890 --> 00:19:16.050
Okay, everyone, step right up.

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:17.650
Aya-chan!

00:19:17.650 --> 00:19:18.870
I'll help you out until this evening.

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:20.550
Our hero!

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:21.920
Hurry it up!

00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:23.630
Yes, right away!

00:19:25.670 --> 00:19:28.490
Yes, the usual Federation of Economic

00:19:28.490 --> 00:19:30.590
Organizations and Diet members,

00:19:30.590 --> 00:19:34.280
and it would be ideal if the Deputy 
Prime Minister would come, too.

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:36.530
Okay, let's go with that.

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:43.100
They look pretty busy.

00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:47.110
I have to find Hasegawa-kun 
as quickly as possible.

00:19:58.370 --> 00:19:59.950
You've gotten used to that.

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:02.590
Just call me a pre-chewing artisan.

00:20:02.590 --> 00:20:05.190
I think we can call this 
one a pretty rare batch.

00:20:05.190 --> 00:20:08.100
Yeah. Looks like we'll be 
making a profit this time.

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:52.950
Moyashimon

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:52.950
Returns

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:52.950
Episode 5

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:52.950
Microbe 
Theater

00:21:50.400 --> 00:21:52.950
Microbe Theater Returns!

00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:52.950
Returns

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:59.080
Keep on brewing!

00:22:01.790 --> 00:22:03.610
This time, we'll tell 
you about the pulque

00:22:03.610 --> 00:22:05.550
that Kawahama and Misato were making.

00:22:05.780 --> 00:22:09.780
Maguey (AKA Agave)

00:22:06.780 --> 00:22:09.150
First, the center stalk 
of a type of agave

00:22:09.150 --> 00:22:11.470
called maguey is broken off,

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:15.050
and the sugary sap inside is drawn out.

00:22:15.050 --> 00:22:16.890
Then we natural yeasts and lactic

00:22:16.890 --> 00:22:19.540
acid bacteria brew it up, and that's it.

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:32.330
About One Week Later

00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:23.800
The pulque is finished in about a week.

00:22:23.800 --> 00:22:25.490
Piece of cake!

00:22:28.180 --> 00:22:29.730
Since it's so easy to make,

00:22:29.730 --> 00:22:32.330
locals have been drinking 
it for over 1,000 years!

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:35.190
By the way, it's said 
that pulque accounts for

00:22:35.190 --> 00:22:39.990
a quarter of Mexico's 
total alcohol consumption.

00:22:40.970 --> 00:22:42.290
Wow!

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:45.400
But to think liquor could be 
made from something like this!

00:22:46.440 --> 00:22:50.200
Those humans will make 
liquor out of anything!
